{"seconds": 59.1, "exit": 0, "final": "White can play Rxe4, and then Black cannot recover. So Qf5+ is the killer move, and it's completely winning in all lines. Now let me write this up concisely.\n\n**Best move:** Qf5+\n\n**Main line:** Qf5+ Kg8 (if Kh8 Rh5#; if Bg6 Qxf2 winning the queen) Qxf7+ Kh8 Rh5#\n\n**Motif:** fork (the queen on f5 gives check to the king and attacks both the queen on f2 and the bishop on f7)\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your opponent's king lacks escape squares, look for forcing checks that attack multiple pieces. Here, Qf5+ checks the king while forking the queen and bishop. After Kg8 (the only try), Qxf7+ drives the king to h8, where Rh5 is unstoppable mate. This teaches us to scan checks first\u2014they often hide the solution.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qf5+\", \"line\": [\"Qf5+\", \"Kg8\", \"Qxf7+\", \"Kh8\", \"Rh5#\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qxg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Rh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Re8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6